message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "To hand off your work from a terminal session to a cloud session in Vibe Code Web, use the `/teleport` command inside an active local session. This moves the session into a Vibe Code Web sandbox, allowing you to continue working remotely without keeping your terminal open.\n\n```text\n/teleport\n```\n\nWhen you run this command, the session continues in Vibe Code Web, which you can monitor from any device signed in to Vibe. You can review the progress, command output, and steer the agent from the web interface.\n\nBy using the web editor surface, you give up direct access to your local files, terminal, and any local secrets or unsupported runtimes. The web session runs in a managed sandbox and works directly against the GitHub repository, producing branches and pull requests for review [1][3][8][9].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "You can start a session in the CLI and resume it in the extension, or the other way around, without losing context. To hand off work to Vibe Code Web, use the `/teleport` command from the CLI."
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "It fits tasks that: Run remotely without local files, services, or secrets."
    },
    {
      "n": 8,
      "quote": "Teleport moves a CLI session into a Vibe Code Web sandbox so the task can keep running without your terminal staying open."
    },
    {
      "n": 9,
      "quote": "The session continues in Vibe Code Web, powered by Mistral Medium 3.5. You can monitor it from any device signed in to Vibe."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

