message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "If a Workspace in Studio reaches its monthly spending limit, API access for that Workspace is suspended until the next month begins or an admin increases the limit. This means that users in that Workspace will not be able to make API requests, and any requests made will return a `429 Too Many Requests` error. However, other Workspaces in the Organization continue to operate normally, as the limit is applied only to the specific Workspace that reached its cap [2, 3, 5].\n\nRegarding the second part of the question, a Workspace spending limit **cannot** exceed the Organization spending limit. The Organization spending limit acts as a ceiling, and Workspace limits must be set to a value that is less than or equal to the Organization limit. If a Workspace limit is set higher than the Organization limit, the Organization limit becomes the effective ceiling [2, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9].\n\nHere is the code to set a monthly spending limit for a Workspace from the Admin Panel:\n\n```bash\n# This is a reference to the Admin Panel action, not an API call\n1. Open [Admin Panel > Administration > Workspaces](https://admin.mistral.ai/organization/workspaces).\n2. Select the Workspace.\n3. Open the **Settings** tab.\n4. Set **Monthly spending limit** to your desired value.\n5. Save your changes.\n```\n\nTo set the Organization's monthly spending limit via the Admin API, you can use the following command:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.mistral.ai/v1/admin/spend-limit \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"x-api-key: $ADMIN_API_KEY\" \\\n  -d '{\"amount\": 500, \"no_monthly_limit\": false}'\n```\n\nThis sets the Organization's spending limit to 500 units of your Organization's billing currency.",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "If the Organization reaches its monthly spending limit, API access can be suspended until the next month begins or an admin increases the limit."
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "If a Workspace reaches its monthly spending limit, API access for that Workspace is suspended until the next month begins or an admin increases the limit."
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "quote": "If a Workspace reaches its monthly spending limit, API access for that Workspace is suspended until the next month begins or the limit is increased."
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "quote": "Workspace spending limits cannot exceed it."
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "quote": "The Organization policy sets the ceiling. Workspace Admins can set a stricter, shorter maximum for their Workspace, but they cannot set a maximum that exceeds the Organization limit."
    },
    {
      "n": 8,
      "quote": "The Organization maximum becomes the effective ceiling for newly created API keys."
    },
    {
      "n": 9,
      "quote": "The Organization policy is the ceiling. Workspace limits can be stricter, but they cannot exceed the Organization maximum."
    },
    {
      "n": 10,
      "quote": "curl -X POST https://api.mistral.ai/v1/admin/spend-limit \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"x-api-key: $ADMIN_API_KEY\" \\\n  -d '{\"amount\": 500, \"no_monthly_limit\": false}'"
    },
    {
      "n": 11,
      "quote": "When the workspace hits the limit, API requests return `429 Too Many Requests` until the next billing cycle."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

