REFERENCE ANSWER
It requires the path parameter `file_id`, a required string (uuid) identifying the file. On success it returns `200` with the file's binary content as `application/octet-stream`.

ANSWER UNDER TEST
The `GET /v1/files/{file_id}/content` (Download File) operation requires the `file_id` parameter, which is part of the URL path. On success, it returns the file content as a stream or bytes, depending on the client used. 

